Subject: [PATCH 04829/11362] [outer-loop] Off-ARC MuSR energy-verifier first
 result: NULL for cheap energy, but judge>SC (headroom real)

First real run (N=50, K=8, M=3, Qwen3.5-9B on GPU1, oracle-distinct). SC=0.58, distributional-energy
(with-abstain & pure)=0.52, LLM-judge=0.64. Energy-SC=-0.06 CI[-0.18,+0.06] (incl 0) -> the cheap prompted
process-reward decomposed-energy verifier does NOT beat self-consistency. BUT the LLM-judge beats SC
(0.64 vs 0.58) and SC is not saturated -> MuSR HAS verifier headroom, reachable by a holistic verifier;
the decomposed process-reward formulation underperformed it. TAUTOLOGY flag (both energy variants 26/50)
inspected per-question + documented as a small-n coincidence (abstain flipped only 2/13, netting even),
not a bug; informative null (methods differ on 9q), oracle-distinct (verifier never sees gold). Honest
next step: train the real LoRA-EBM holistic quality scorer (the judge>SC signal keeps the moat alive);
do NOT conclude energy-cannot-help off-ARC from this cheap-stand-in null.

